\n=== BRIEF 08 RULES (first 80 lines) ===
     1	## Investigation Brief 08 — Exception Flags (Part II) and Artifacts
     2	
     3	Controller memo (binding reconciliation rule):
     4	
     5	Continued from Brief 07. Set `policy_waiver` when final status is `approved`,
     6	`amount_usd` > 10000, and a Policy Exception block exists for that transaction
     7	with `approved_by: compliance` on its own line. Set `retroactive_review` when
     8	final status is `reversed`, `amount_usd` > 5000, and a winning correction
     9	notice changed status for that transaction.
    10	
    11	`extract --outdir` must write: `transactions.json` as `{"items":[...]}` sorted
    12	by `transaction_id` ascending with fields transaction_id, owner, status
    13	(lowercase), effective_date, amount_usd, exception_reason (null or
    14	semicolon-joined codes). `transactions.csv` uses header
    15	transaction_id,owner,status,effective_date,amount_usd,exception_reason with the
    16	same rows; leave exception_reason blank when null. `exceptions.json` is
    17	`{"items":[...]}` with only rows where exception_reason is set.
    18	`reconciliation_report.jsonl` is one JSON object per winning correction with
    19	notice_id, transaction_id, field, previous_value, new_value, effective, sorted
    20	by notice_id ascending.
    21	
